---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Istanbul to Burgas: Travel Guide for Eurovision 2027" 
  description="The ultimate guide to traveling from Istanbul to Burgas for Eurovision 2027. Compare direct buses, private VIP transfers, and flight options."
  breadcrumb="Istanbul to Burgas"
>
  <div class="container page-content">
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <h1 class="text-gradient" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">How to Travel from Istanbul to Burgas for Eurovision 2027</h1>
      
      <p class="lead" style="font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 40px; color: var(--text-muted);">
        Istanbul (IST or SAW) is the closest major global aviation hub to Burgas. If you are flying in from outside Europe (UK, Americas, Australia, Asia), flying into Istanbul and crossing the border to Bulgaria is often the fastest and cheapest route.
      </p>

      <div class="glass-panel mb-4">
        <h2>Option 1: Private VIP Transfer (Recommended)</h2>
        <p>If you are traveling with a group of 3 or more, a private transfer is the most comfortable and efficient way to reach your hotel in Burgas directly from the Istanbul arrivals hall.</p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
          <li><strong>Time:</strong> ~4.5 hours (depending on border control)</li>
          <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Door-to-door, skips bus station hassle, flexible departure time.</li>
          <li><strong>Vehicles:</strong> Mercedes V-Class or premium sedans.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/vip-transfers" class="btn btn-primary">Get a VIP Transfer Quote</a>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-panel mb-4">
        <h2>Option 2: Direct Bus from Istanbul Esenler</h2>
        <p>Several bus companies (Nishikli, Arda Tur, Metro) run daily routes from Istanbul's main bus terminal (Esenler Otogar) directly to Burgas Bus Station South.</p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
          <li><strong>Time:</strong> ~5-6 hours</li>
          <li><strong>Cost:</strong> ~€25 - €35</li>
          <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Very affordable, modern buses with Wi-Fi and AC.</li>
          <li><strong>Cons:</strong> You must travel from the airport to the bus terminal first. Border crossing takes longer when an entire bus of passports needs processing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Pro-Tip:</em> Book your tickets well in advance for May 2027, as buses will sell out fast around the Eurovision dates.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-panel mb-4" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-amber);">
        <h3>Important Border Crossing Info (Malko Tarnovo / Dereköy)</h3>
        <p>You will cross a physical, non-Schengen land border between Turkey and Bulgaria. Ensure you have:</p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 16px;">
          <li>A valid multiple-entry Schengen Visa, Bulgarian Visa, or a passport with visa-free access to Bulgaria.</li>
          <li>Printed hotel confirmations (sometimes requested by border guards).</li>
          <li>Patience! The border crossing usually takes 30-60 minutes, but can stretch longer if multiple buses arrive simultaneously.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content {
    padding: 64px 24px;
  }
  
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.8rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  
  h2 {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  
  li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
